# Netlify redirect rules.
#
# NOTHING IS ENABLED HERE YET, ON PURPOSE.
#
# Star Stuff learned on 2026-08-15 that Netlify does not send the .netlify.app
# hostname to the custom domain on its own: four addresses answered HTTP 200 with
# byte-identical documents. The fix is a forced host redirect, and this file will
# carry the same one.
#
# It cannot be turned on yet. As of 2026-09-07 `queering.earth` is not registered
# — whois.nic.earth returns "No Data Found" — so the only address this site has is
# the .netlify.app one. Enabling the rule below now would redirect the live site
# to a domain that does not resolve, which is a site that is simply down.
#
# ENABLE THIS the same day the custom domain is attached in Netlify, and not before:
#
# http://queering-earth.netlify.app/*   https://queering.earth/:splat  301!
# https://queering-earth.netlify.app/*  https://queering.earth/:splat  301!
#
# The hostname above is confirmed: the Netlify project is `queering-earth`
# (id 4115815c-5811-4df6-8f6f-9598e85d2d72, Stimpunks team), serving
# https://queering-earth.netlify.app since 2026-09-07.
